(I)--a daughter of दक्ष and one of the wives of तैक्ष्य, (कश्यप-म्। प्।, वा। प्।, वि। प्।), begot गरुड and अरुण (see also सुपर्णा);
1: Br. III. 3. ५६; 7. २९ and ४६८; ६१. ४२; भा. III. १५. ४०; VI. 6. २१-2; M. 6. 2, ३३-4; १४६. १८ and २२; १७१. २९ and ६२; वा. ६६. ५४; Vi. I. १५. १२५.
known for flying in the air;
2: वा. ६९. ८३.
had [page३-238+ २२] two sons and thirtysix daughters; they comprised the गायत्री and other छन्दस् and birds like सुपर्णा;
3: Ib. ६९. ६६-7.

(I)--a Mt. (Kulaparvata-वा। प्।) in भारत vars2a. Here दक्ष performed tapas;
1: भा. V. १९. १६; VI. 4. २०; Vi. II. 3. 3.
a Kulaparvata sacred for श्राद्ध offerings.
2: Br. II, १६. १९; III. 7. ३५६; १३. ३४; M. ११४. १८; वा. ४५. ८९; ५८. ८१; ६९. २३९; ७७. ३४; ८८. १९९; ९६. ३८.
Here Haihaya came for hunting: कृष्ण went there in search of Prasena;
3: Br. III. २६. २५; ७१. ३९.
sacred to विन्द्याधि- वासिनी and the पितृस्;
4: M. १३. ३९; २२. ६६.
caused by Agastya to bow down and not to rise in height;
5: Ib. ६१. ५१.
joining with the Ganges is more sacred than कुरुक्षेत्र;
6: Ib. १०६. ४९.
rivers originating from;
7: Ib. ११४. २७-8; वा. ४५. १०३.
obstructed by it the गङ्गा enters the sea;
8: M. १२१. ५१; वा. ४७. ५०.
Goddess of night was asked to seek shelter in the Vindhyas after she left उमा's body.
9: M. १५७, १७, १९.

--a son of Kilakila (कैङ्किल Yavana- वि। प्।) succeeded by वैदिशक kings;
1: Br. III. ७४. १७८.
ruled for ९६ years;
2: वा. ९९. ३६५.
father of पुरञ्जय.
3: Vi. IV. २४. ५६.
